<Placemark>   <name>Castledermot High Crosses</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Co. Kildare <b>Alt Name:</b> St Dairmuid's Cross, <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 52.910416 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -6.834854<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/ireland/Kildare/thumb/bz_P9110760.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Co. Kildare. Castledermot (Dysert Diarmaid) monastic site is 6 miles NE of Carlow. In the churchyard are two 9th century high crosses and a round tower. The site dates back to 815 or ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=27094" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-6.834854,52.910416,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Clonmore</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Co. Carlow <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>4</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>5</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 52.827023236735 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -6.569142845533<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/ireland/Carlow/thumb/FZyHS_aX0AA6V5d.jpeg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    A stunning collection of early Christian crosses and cross slabs n Co. Carlow, plus more dotted about the area including large multiple Bullaun, Ogham stone and more.. There is a large earthfast multi...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=57212" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-6.569142845533,52.827023236735,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Cross of the Scriptures (Clonmacnoise)</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Co. Offaly <b>Alt Name:</b> St Ciaran's Cross, King Flan's Cross <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 53.326442553739 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -7.985879355135<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/ireland/Offaly/thumb/ov_P8310717.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Clonmacnois (Cluain Mhic Nois) the great Celtic monastic site beside the River Shannon, dates from 545 CE when St Ciaran (512-45), from Connaught, founded a monastery here. There are 3 9th century cro...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=27062" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-7.9858793551353,53.326442553739,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
